<h2 id="louisiana-taxes">Louisiana taxes for side hustlers</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>State income tax:</strong> Louisiana moved to a flat 3% income tax starting in 2025, with a much larger standard deduction than before.</li>
  <li><strong>Federal taxes:</strong> you owe federal income tax plus 15.3% self-employment tax on net profit. Plan to set aside 20–25%; the <a href="/tools/self-employment-tax-calculator/">self-employment tax calculator</a> gives a closer number.</li>
  <li><strong>Sales tax:</strong> the state rate rose to 5% in 2025, and parish and city taxes stack on top, putting combined rates among the highest in the country. If you sell crafts or products, you need to collect and remit it.</li>
  <li><strong>Tips count:</strong> casino and hospitality tips are taxable income, so report them accurately.</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Watch out:</strong> Louisiana sales tax is collected at both the state and local level, and Bossier has its own local collector. If you sell at markets, confirm where and how to file before your first event.</div>

